      "content": "**Zenith Smart Hub Error 404: Connectivity Lost Troubleshooting Guide**\n\n**Step 1: Power Cycle the Hub (1 point)**\nImmediately shut down the Zenith Smart Hub by pressing and holding the power button for 10 seconds. Unplug the power cord from the wall outlet. Wait for 30 seconds to allow any residual power to drain. Plug the power cord back into the wall outlet and turn the hub back on.\n\n**Step 2: Verify Power Supply (1 point)**\nEnsure the Zenith Smart Hub is receiving power from the wall outlet. Check the power cord for any signs of damage or wear. Verify that the outlet is functioning properly by plugging in a different device. If using a surge protector, unplug it from the wall outlet and plug it back in to reset the circuit.\n\n**Step 3: Restart Router and Modem (1 point)**\nRestart your router and modem to ensure they are communicating with the Zenith Smart Hub. Unplug the power cord from the router and modem, wait for 30 seconds, and then plug them back in. Verify that the router and modem are receiving power by checking their lights.\n\n**Step 4: Check Network Cables (1 point)**",
